# RAG pipeline

Order is fixed: retrieve top-10 → CrossEncoder rerank → confidence gate → generate.

- Embeddings: `BAAI/bge-m3` (query and passages must use the same model).
- Reranker: `BAAI/bge-reranker-base`.
- Chunks: page-aware; persist `doc_id`, `filename`, `page`, `text`, `language`, `chunk_index`.
- Baseline chunking: 512 tokens, 64 overlap (`docs/decisions.md`).
- If best rerank score < `RERANK_MIN_SCORE`, skip the LLM and return low confidence.
- LLM prompt: answer only from context; match user language when possible (FR/AR/EN).
- Eval belongs in `backend/app/eval/`, not inside `pipeline.py`.

Do not replace this two-stage retrieve+rerank with “just k=5 from Chroma.”
